From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bpereira <bpereira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 20:55:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Compact retained DOM node storage

A node slot paid for data that most nodes never use. Move it out of
line and keep it only where it is needed:

- Image layers with no url keep no image storage; shadow-root data,
  comment contents, template and shadow-root links, pseudo-element links,
  anonymous blocks, list-item data, transforms and the wide special
  element payloads live in boxed side storage that most elements never
  allocate.
- Table cell and row lists, parser growth slack, inline-layout text and
  node-range slack are shrunk once they are built.
- Class atoms are a ThinVec; an element stores its namespace as a byte
  next to its local name, an attribute its prefix and namespace apart
  from its local name; element state, selector flags and boolean flags
  are packed; nullable node ids keep NodeId alignment.
- The opaque-id side table keeps only slot versions, and the document's
  style lock is reached through the node tree instead of per node.
- Element layout state is allocated on first use and shared, and an
  element's inline text layout lives in its layout data.

Readers go through accessors; inherited dir/lang restyles read a parent
through the nullable-id overlay. Layout, paint and serialization output
are unchanged.

Signed-off-by: bpereira <bpereira@cloudflare.com>
